{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And a bribe you shall not take.</b> Even to render true judgment. However, compensation for cancellation of one's work — it is permitted to take from both litigants, in their presence, as Karna would do. <b>And a bribe you shall not take.</b> They placed it here, for it is the custom that the rich man gives the judge a bribe to tilt the judgment against his opponent." "<b>And it will pervert the words of the righteous.</b> And it will change the plea of the righteous and the innocent in judgment, to reverse it against them."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:58.161099690Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}